1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,899
Hello everyone!

2
00:00:01,899 --> 00:00:11,276
Today we're introducing PNCC Care, a family safety app built specifically for seniors living alone and the family members who care for them.

3
00:00:11,276 --> 00:00:18,242
When older parents live by themselves, adult children naturally worry about falls or sudden emergencies.

4
00:00:18,242 --> 00:00:24,137
But installing cameras all over the house feels intrusive and strips away their privacy.

5
00:00:24,137 --> 00:00:34,250
PNCC Care takes a respectful approach: with just one simple tap on a phone or smartwatch each day, parents let their family know they're safe and well.

6
00:00:34,250 --> 00:00:42,863
It works across iPhones, iPads, Apple Watches, and Android devices—simple, straightforward, and ready to use right out of the box.

7
00:00:43,280 --> 00:00:49,115
Many apps look completely different across devices, which easily confuses older users.

8
00:00:49,115 --> 00:00:55,289
PNCC Care uses a unified system that connects phones, tablets, and smartwatches seamlessly.

9
00:00:55,289 --> 00:00:57,731
Best of all, it works offline-first.

10
00:00:57,731 --> 00:01:07,299
Even if home Wi-Fi drops out or someone is in the basement with no signal, tapping the check-in button saves the record safely on the device.

11
00:01:07,299 --> 00:01:13,135
As soon as the connection returns, it automatically syncs with the rest of the family.

12
00:01:13,135 --> 00:01:21,888
It uses less than 2 kilobytes of data a day and barely sips battery, so even older smartphones run it smoothly without slowdowns.

13
00:01:22,680 --> 00:01:26,013
Family connection should be effortless yet secure.

14
00:01:26,013 --> 00:01:29,212
PNCC Care offers flexible bidirectional linking.

15
00:01:29,212 --> 00:01:39,414
In person, it works either way: children can scan the senior's QR code to join their care circle, or parents can scan their child's code to grant access.

16
00:01:39,414 --> 00:01:48,814
For long-distance families where scanning isn't possible, children can simply search by the parent's name or user ID and send a care request.

17
00:01:48,814 --> 00:02:01,216
To strictly protect elderly privacy, no one can link uninvited: a pending request pops up on the senior's phone, requiring their explicit tap of approval before any status can be viewed.

18
00:02:02,040 --> 00:02:08,021
Everyone in a family has different needs, so an app shouldn't look the same for everyone.

19
00:02:08,021 --> 00:02:10,575
PNCC Care features two distinct modes.

20
00:02:10,575 --> 00:02:18,707
For older parents, 'Senior Safe Mode' strips away all confusing menus and buttons, leaving only giant, friendly controls.

21
00:02:18,707 --> 00:02:27,043
For adult children or caregivers, the 'Caregiver Console' displays an overview of all family members on one clean dashboard.

22
00:02:27,043 --> 00:02:35,512
You can switch between them with one tap, giving seniors effortless simplicity while giving caregivers complete peace of mind.

23
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:39,677
Here is the daily home screen seniors interact with.

24
00:02:39,677 --> 00:02:47,296
Right across the center is a full-width rounded rectangular emerald green button that clearly says 'I'm OK · Check In.

25
00:02:47,296 --> 00:02:55,173
' Unlike small circular buttons where seniors with trembling fingers or weak eyesight might miss the target, PNCC Care v1.

26
00:02:55,173 --> 00:02:56,673
1.

27
00:02:56,673 --> 00:03:03,452
5 features a full-width rectangular bar spanning the entire screen with a generous 60-point touch height.

28
00:03:03,452 --> 00:03:08,424
Parents can comfortably tap anywhere across the bar without aiming carefully.

29
00:03:08,424 --> 00:03:17,592
Every morning after getting out of bed, one light tap triggers a gentle haptic buzz and switches to a reassuring checkmark saying 'Safe Today.

30
00:03:17,592 --> 00:03:25,984
' At the exact same second, family members—even if they're miles away at work—get an instant notification that their loved one is safe and sound.

31
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:33,479
What happens if a parent sleeps in or steps out for a morning walk and misses the scheduled check-in time?

32
00:03:33,479 --> 00:03:36,686
Does the phone immediately trigger panic alarms?

33
00:03:36,686 --> 00:03:38,186
Not at all.

34
00:03:38,186 --> 00:03:41,191
We designed a gentle 25-minute buffer period.

35
00:03:41,191 --> 00:03:48,806
During this window, the green button turns into a warm amber reminder, gently asking the parent to tap when ready.

36
00:03:48,806 --> 00:03:55,217
The app doesn't blast loud sirens or send frightening alerts to family members during this time.

37
00:03:55,217 --> 00:04:02,000
It simply nudges the senior with a warm visual prompt, avoiding false alarms while keeping safety on track.

38
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:08,699
Beyond physical safety, emotional and spiritual well-being is just as meaningful for older adults.

39
00:04:08,699 --> 00:04:18,535
After completing their daily check-in, seniors see a daily Bible verse appear right below the button, such as 'The Lord is my shepherd; I shall not want.

40
00:04:18,535 --> 00:04:22,071
' Tapping the card opens a full, built-in Bible reader.

41
00:04:22,071 --> 00:04:30,685
The complete text is stored directly on the device, so parents can browse chapters offline anytime without waiting for slow downloads.

42
00:04:30,685 --> 00:04:36,663
The font sizes and line spacing are enlarged specifically to protect older eyes from fatigue.

43
00:04:37,479 --> 00:04:41,664
What if an older adult slips at home or feels sudden chest pain?

44
00:04:41,664 --> 00:04:46,896
In the upper corner of the senior screen, there is a dedicated red 'SOS' button.

45
00:04:46,896 --> 00:04:53,044
The senior doesn't need to unlock their phone, open contacts, or search through phone numbers.

46
00:04:53,044 --> 00:05:00,565
Holding the SOS button for three seconds immediately places a direct phone call to their primary emergency contact.

47
00:05:00,565 --> 00:05:10,375
At the same time, top-priority alert notifications are sent to all designated family members, putting help just seconds away when every second counts.

48
00:05:11,199 --> 00:05:13,840
Now let's switch to the caregiver's view.

49
00:05:13,840 --> 00:05:22,797
If you are caring for both your father and mother, or if you're a volunteer checking on neighbors, this monitoring matrix is indispensable.

50
00:05:22,797 --> 00:05:33,365
Each card represents one senior: green means 'checked in safely today,' amber means 'nearing deadline or in buffer period,' and red highlights an 'overdue check-in.

51
00:05:33,365 --> 00:05:39,873
' Each card clearly displays the person's name, their exact check-in time, and how much time remains.

52
00:05:39,873 --> 00:05:44,191
You can see who is safe and who needs attention in a single glance.

53
00:05:44,999 --> 00:05:53,124
If a family member notices a senior's card turning yellow or red, clicking on that card brings up a quick-action drawer.

54
00:05:53,124 --> 00:06:08,022
There are two primary shortcuts: 'Direct Call,' which instantly rings the senior's phone, and 'Preset SMS,' which opens a gentle text message saying, 'Hi Mom, just checking in—please remember to tap your check-in button!

55
00:06:08,022 --> 00:06:13,236
' It's respectful, warm, and requires no copying or pasting of phone numbers.

56
00:06:13,236 --> 00:06:15,470
Communication takes just one tap.

57
00:06:16,279 --> 00:06:19,507
Seniors have vastly different daily routines.

58
00:06:19,507 --> 00:06:26,536
Some wake up at 6:00 AM for morning exercise, while others need more rest and sleep until 9:00 AM.

59
00:06:26,536 --> 00:06:29,475
PNCC Care avoids one-size-fits-all rules.

60
00:06:29,475 --> 00:06:33,492
Each senior can have their own custom check-in deadline.

61
00:06:33,492 --> 00:06:41,812
In the settings menu, family members can spin a time wheel to set the deadline to 8:00 AM, 9:30 AM, or even evening.

62
00:06:41,812 --> 00:06:49,271
The app adapts completely to the senior's natural circadian rhythm rather than interrupting their sleep.

63
00:06:50,079 --> 00:06:56,643
For safety alerts, PNCC Care uses a dependable Dual-Timer and Emergency Escalation architecture.

64
00:06:56,643 --> 00:07:02,523
Timer 1 governs the senior's local check-in frequency with gentle on-device reminders.

65
00:07:02,523 --> 00:07:14,350
Timer 2 is the caregiver alert timeout, which must be set longer than Timer 1, notifying family only when inactivity truly exceeds safe thresholds to eliminate false alarms.

66
00:07:14,350 --> 00:07:21,802
If caregivers do not acknowledge the critical alert, the system can escalate to prepare a 911 emergency call.

67
00:07:21,802 --> 00:07:28,639
Combined with hardware fall detection and shake-to-panic, it ensures real safety when seconds count.

68
00:07:29,439 --> 00:07:38,165
Many older adults deal with cataracts, glaucoma, or severe presbyopia, making standard phone text nearly impossible to read.

69
00:07:38,165 --> 00:07:43,515
PNCC Care follows the highest international accessibility standard—WCAG AAA.

70
00:07:43,515 --> 00:07:52,100
In the accessibility settings, users can drag a font size slider to enlarge text up to more than double its standard size.

71
00:07:52,100 --> 00:08:05,192
We also built an OLED high-contrast mode with a pitch-black background and bright white typography, achieving a 12:1 contrast ratio that remains crystal clear even under bright sunlight.

72
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:12,463
When parents travel on vacation with family or stay in the hospital, daily check-ins aren't needed.

73
00:08:12,463 --> 00:08:23,369
With 'Vacation Mode,' users simply pick start and end dates to pause all countdowns and reminders, letting everyone enjoy their trip without unnecessary notifications.

74
00:08:23,369 --> 00:08:28,201
Regarding privacy, we adhere to strict global privacy standards like GDPR.

75
00:08:28,201 --> 00:08:39,759
If a family ever decides to stop using the service, one tap on 'Erase All Data' permanently removes all personal records from both the device and cloud servers in three seconds.

76
00:08:40,560 --> 00:08:49,115
On larger screens like iPads or Android tablets, PNCC Care automatically transforms into a desktop-grade monitoring dashboard.

77
00:08:49,115 --> 00:08:53,121
On an iPad Pro, it presents an efficient split-view layout.

78
00:08:53,121 --> 00:09:05,546
The left pane hosts up to a 4-column grid showing real-time status cards for dozens of seniors at once, while the right pane shows detailed history, timelines, and emergency contacts.

79
00:09:05,546 --> 00:09:15,256
During an emergency, a full-screen dispatch card appears, making it an ideal central command station for nursing homes or community volunteers.

80
00:09:16,080 --> 00:09:22,714
Seniors often leave their phones charging in another room, but a smartwatch stays right on their wrist.

81
00:09:22,714 --> 00:09:25,806
PNCC Care includes a standalone Apple Watch app.

82
00:09:25,806 --> 00:09:33,729
When parents wake up in the morning, they simply glance at their wrist and tap the green checkmark to confirm they're safe.

83
00:09:33,729 --> 00:09:38,689
If a check-in is pending, the watch delivers gentle haptic taps on the wrist.

84
00:09:38,689 --> 00:09:48,352
In case of an emergency, pressing the red SOS button on the watch face calls for help immediately, providing continuous protection wherever they walk.

85
00:09:49,160 --> 00:09:54,391
We pushed convenience to its absolute limit: you don't even have to open the app.

86
00:09:54,391 --> 00:10:00,526
On both iPhone lock screens and home screens, you can place dedicated PNCC Care status widgets.

87
00:10:00,526 --> 00:10:06,856
The widgets feature clean color rings and status labels showing whether mom or dad has checked in.

88
00:10:06,856 --> 00:10:14,799
When a deadline is approaching, the Dynamic Island on modern iPhones displays a live status capsule with a countdown timer.

89
00:10:14,799 --> 00:10:21,000
Whether you're reading emails or browsing the web, a quick glance gives you total peace of mind.

90
00:10:21,800 --> 00:10:31,563
At bedtime, when a senior places their iPhone horizontally on a nightstand charger, PNCC Care automatically transitions into StandBy Ambient Mode.

91
00:10:31,563 --> 00:10:37,783
The screen turns into an oversized digital clock displaying the current time and safe status.

92
00:10:37,783 --> 00:10:44,671
In a dark room, the display shifts to a warm red hue that won't disrupt sleep or strain sensitive eyes.

93
00:10:44,671 --> 00:10:50,222
If the senior wakes up in the middle of the night, the time is visible at a glance.

94
00:10:50,222 --> 00:10:55,104
It's a reliable safety guard by day and a calming bedside clock by night.

95
00:10:55,920 --> 00:11:05,564
In critical emergencies—such as an urgent SOS call or extended unresponsiveness—PNCC Care's four-platform alert network springs into full action.

96
00:11:05,564 --> 00:11:13,346
Family members' iPhones receive critical alerts that bypass mute switches and focus modes, sounding an audible alarm.

97
00:11:13,346 --> 00:11:22,924
Tablets display an urgent dispatch card, Android phones show high-priority heads-up banners, and smartwatches vibrate persistently on the wrist.

98
00:11:22,924 --> 00:11:29,776
Even if family members are in silent meetings or asleep, they won't miss this life-saving notification.

99
00:11:30,600 --> 00:11:39,217
In conclusion, PNCC Care isn't just another cold tech utility; it's a digital bridge built on love, dignity, and family connection.

100
00:11:39,217 --> 00:11:46,453
It doesn't require expensive hardware, it never invades personal privacy, and it involves zero learning curve.

101
00:11:46,453 --> 00:11:52,242
With one humble daily tap, it connects a parent's well-being with their children's care.

102
00:11:52,242 --> 00:12:02,175
We are committed to transparent open-source software so that every older adult can age with dignity, and every family can live with true peace of mind.

103
00:12:02,175 --> 00:12:03,688
Thank you for watching!
